From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:09:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: msm_sdhci: keep SDR12 timing for eMMC high speed

msm_sdhci uses the generic sdhci_set_control_reg(), which programs the
HOST_CONTROL2 UHS mode select field with SDR25 for MMC_HS and SDR50 for
MMC_HS_52. The Linux sdhci-msm driver programs that field only for UHS,
HS200, HS400 and DDR timings and leaves eMMC high speed at SDR12 (0).

On the Eliza CQS EVK (SDCC core version 1, minor 0x72) the eMMC is
identified and the first EXT_CSD read after the switch to 8-bit high
speed works, but once the host clock is raised to 52 MHz with SDR50
selected the card's responses are missed, the card is left in the data
state and every later command times out, so no partition can be read:

  CMD_SEND:6  ARG 0x03b90100  MMC_RSP_R1b 0x0000000b
  CMD_SEND:8  ARG 0x00000000  RET -110
  mmc0 busy timeout
  unable to select a mode: -70

The same failure shows with a 4-bit bus and with the controller clocked
at 50 MHz without the SDHCI divider, while legacy timing (high speed cap
masked) reads the eMMC. With SDR12 for MMC_HS and MMC_HS_52, as Linux
programs it, the card runs in 8-bit HS52 and U-Boot loads the OS from
it.

This applies to every msm_sdhci eMMC that ends in HS or HS52, which
without HS200 support in qcom_defconfig is most of them. eMMCs that
select DDR52 keep the DDR50 code, as in Linux.

[port: qualcomm-linux u-boot already has sdhci_msm_set_control_reg();
 the SDR12 case is added to it instead of a new set_control_reg op; its
 qcom_defconfig enables HS200 and HS400, so here the change applies to
 the eMMCs U-Boot runs at HS52, such as the Eliza CQS EVK's, where
 HS400 and HS200 tuning fail (the DLL does not lock) and U-Boot falls
 back to HS52]

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/mmc/msm_sdhci.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/msm_sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/msm_sdhci.c
index 155bc2ef379..d5f423548c3 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/msm_sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/msm_sdhci.c
@@ -819,6 +819,19 @@ static void sdhci_msm_set_control_reg(struct sdhci_host *host)
 		ctrl2 &= ~SDHCI_CTRL_UHS_MASK;
 		ctrl2 |= SDHCI_CTRL_UHS_SDR104;
 		sdhci_writew(host, ctrl2, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
+	} else if (mmc->selected_mode == MMC_HS ||
+		   mmc->selected_mode == MMC_HS_52) {
+		u32 ctrl2 = sdhci_readw(host, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
+
+		/*
+		 * eMMC high speed is not a UHS mode: keep the UHS field at
+		 * SDR12, as the kernel driver does. With the SDR25/SDR50 codes
+		 * the generic code picks, the controller misses the card's
+		 * responses once the clock is raised.
+		 */
+		ctrl2 &= ~SDHCI_CTRL_UHS_MASK;
+		ctrl2 |= SDHCI_CTRL_UHS_SDR12;
+		sdhci_writew(host, ctrl2, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
 	} else {
 		sdhci_set_uhs_timing(host);
 	}
-- 
